/-!
# The P48p catalogue pairing frame

The integral Gram matrix `G` and the generators `a, b, d` in their listed order
come from the Nebe–Sloane Catalogue of Lattices, P48p entry, sections GRAM and
GROUP_GENERATORS.
<https://www.math.rwth-aachen.de/~Gabriele.Nebe/LATTICES/P48p.html>

The catalogue HTML SHA-256 is
`eaec7003064f5a0ed7c0cb96dd37374fe6ef51e086f40422ec8422df9cf6111a`.
The frame rows `U` come from the FIFO orbit starting at

    [1, 1, 3, -2, -1, 1, 0, 1, 2, 3, 0, 0, -4, 2, 1, -1,
     -2, 2, -1, 0, 2, -1, 1, -1, -1, -2, 1, 1, 1, -1, -1, -2,
     -2, 1, -1, 0, 1, 1, 1, 0, 1, -1, -2, 0, 0, 1, -1, 0]

by right multiplication with `[b, a²d, abd, ada², da, dba²]`, in that order.
Of the 96 encountered rows, keep those whose first nonzero entry is positive,
in encounter order. The SHA-256 of the resulting table (space-separated decimal
entries, LF between rows, no final LF) is
`f5592de648c6df07179234bb8592d49ff6a38768e79a079d1bfcb0b4dc900f63`.
The columns of `F = G * Uᵀ` give the pairings with those rows.
-/

